# Lockfiles are derived state and are never hand-merged. On conflict, git
# keeps the current side wholesale (the built-in "ours" driver) instead of
# emitting conflict markers into 3,000 lines of YAML nobody wrote by hand.
# The step that makes this correct: run `pnpm install` afterwards so the
# resolver re-derives the file from the already-merged package.json — the
# lockfile that lands must always be one the resolver wrote.
pnpm-lock.yaml merge=ours

# The golden theme files are compared with the build's output BYTE FOR BYTE
# (packages/design-system/tools/check-golden.ts). `-text` tells git never to
# convert their line endings: on a checkout with core.autocrlf on they would
# otherwise arrive as CRLF, and every theme would fail a gate it had not broken.
packages/design-system/tools/golden/*.css -text
